 "note": "BAC only: Banco Nacional's site didn't answer and Banco de Costa Rica's home page links no card tariff a plain request reaches; BAC is among the country's largest card issuers. BAC Costa Rica's credit card tariff (in force from 3 July 2026), read in full, with its card catalogue (read 30 October 2026) for the cards' names: the tariff gives a total annual rate in colones of 35.88% for its loyalty-program cards, 24.00% for the Óptima (written under its tariff name, Tarjeta de Crédito Óptima) and 31.44% for The Platinum Card Metal. Every card in the catalogue earns cash back, miles or points, so each is written at the loyalty-program rate, except the two EconoMía cards, whose program the catalogue doesn't make clear and which the tariff doesn't name, so they aren't written; where the catalogue gives an American Express and a Visa card the same name (avianca Lifemiles Gold and Premium) one is written. BAC charges no account administration or membership fee, nothing for a cash advance, an overdraft of the limit or a purchase abroad (written as a 0% foreign transaction fee), and no moratory interest. Its late charge, 5% of the overdue part of the principal, at most 12 dollars, has a ceiling in another currency and isn't written. No minimum payment or grace period is stated.",
